c. educational assistance for women victims of violence who are withdrawn from education; and

d. fostering and enhancing the economic independence of women victims of violence.

Article 5

(1) Every woman has the right to:

a. live and maintain her life, and improve the level of welfare in her life;
b. practice religious teachings in accordance with Islamic sharia;
c. obtain justice, security, and freedom to express opinions without discrimination;
d. obtain protection of her personal self, family, honor, dignity and property rights;
e. fulfill her basic needs to grow and develop properly, have a family and continue her lineage;

I

f. obtain fair and equal treatment in carrying out her roles and functions both in family life, society and fully participate in every process of making, determining and implementing development policies;

g. obtain education and teaching in all types, levels, and pathways of education, without any obstacles or pressure in order to improve her skills and quality of life;

h. obtain information and knowledge for women about health, especially comprehensive reproductive health; and i. obtain special protection in carrying out work or profession against matters that threaten her safety and/or health concerning reproductive function.

(2) Every woman in her capacity as a wife, while in a marital bond, has the same rights and responsibilities as her husband over all matters concerning her marital life, relationship with her children, and ownership and management of joint property in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.

(3) In addition to the rights as referred to in paragraph (2), a woman as a wife is entitled to receive material and spiritual support from her husband.

(4) After the dissolution of marriage, a woman has rights and responsibilities from her former husband over all matters concerning children, taking into account the best interests of the child.

Article 9

Implementation of protection of women is provided to:

a. women as housewives;
b. women heads of household;
c. women domestic workers;
d. women workers/laborers;
e. women with disabilities;
f. women homeless;
g. women former inmates of correctional institutions;
h. women victims of violence;
i. Women victims of conflict; and
j. elderly women.

Article 6

Every woman with disabilities is entitled to obtain: a. education in all units, pathways, types, and levels of education; b. decent work and livelihood in accordance with the type and degree of disability, education, and ability;

c. equal treatment to participate in development and enjoy its results;

d. accessibility in the context of her independence;

e. rehabilitation, social assistance, and maintenance of social welfare standards; f. equal rights to develop talents, abilities, and social life; and

g. other rights as regulated in laws and regulations.

