Article 35

(1) The District Government encourages the business sector to participate in the protection of women from acts of violence.

(2) Such participation is carried out both internally and externally.

(3) Internal participation as referred to in paragraph (2) may take the form of: a. socialization to employees within the company regarding the dangers of acts of violence against women;

b. building an internal women's system to handle issues of violence against women; and

c. providing social assistance as a form of corporate social responsibility.

(4) External participation as referred to in paragraph (2) may take the form of: a. providing special opportunities for women victims of violence to work in the company;

b. creating special education and training for women victims of violence;

c. educational assistance for women victims of violence who are withdrawn from education; and

d. fostering and enhancing the economic independence of women victims of violence.

Article 25

(1) The Regency Government has obligations and responsibilities to carry out efforts to prevent violence against women in the form of:

a. collecting data and information about victims of violence and laws and regulations;
b. conducting education on anti-violence values against women;
c. socializing laws and regulations related to the provision of protection for victims of violence;
d. fostering support from religious leaders and traditional leaders to build public awareness of the importance of protecting women;
e. monitoring and evaluating the provision of protection for victims of violence; and
f. preparing reports on the provision of protection for women victims of violence.
(2) To anticipate acts of violence against women, the Regency Government has the obligation to provide and organize services for victims in the form of:
a. establishing institutions and facilitating the provision of integrated services for victims involving community elements; and b. encouraging public awareness of the importance of protecting victims.
(3) To prevent acts of violence against women, the Regency Government carries out the following efforts:
a. conducting socialization regarding regulations and policies relating to violence against women for gampong apparatus, traditional leaders and religious leaders;
b. providing counseling to immediately report to local authorities if violence against women occurs;
c. forming a network in efforts to prevent violence; and d. other efforts deemed strategic to prevent violence against women.

